{
  "longTitle": "To abolish control orders and make provision for the imposition of terrorism prevention and investigation measures.",
  "summary": "<p>The provisions in the Bill follow on from the Coalition Government&rsquo;s 'Review of Counter-Terrorism and Security Powers', published in January 2011.</p><p>The Bill abolishes the system of control orders, established under the Prevention of Terrorism Act 2005, and replaces it with a new regime designed to protect the public from terrorism, called Terrorism Prevention and Investigation Measures.</p>",
